        verification storyAdvisoryInstrumentationDoD : Test { :>> id = "7fa4828f-b8ab-4a74-8670-89a05329a772"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "DELIVERED: dcAdvisoryInstrumentation (resolves issue230 - three panel lenses independently found the zero-advisory-blocks datum uninformative: 1,164 pre-bash fires could mean deterrence or dead weight, and D0197's declared revisit condition was structurally untriggerable). THE FIX, entirely WITHIN the frozen 6-field ledger schema (events are declared vocabulary; fields were not touched, so D0180's freeze holds): an advisory that actually SPEAKS emits advisory-issued, and speaking the SAME advice hash again in the same session emits advisory-repeated - the mechanical ignore signal, tracked per-session under .keel/metrics. All three pre-bash speak paths instrumented (shell-adaptation advisories, blocked-under-strict patterns, human-channel asks). enforcement-report gains advisoryIssued / advisoryRepeated / advisoryApproxHeedPct with its honesty note IN the output: heeded-vs-never-retried is indistinguishable by design, so the rate is stated approximate. control-events.toml declares both events (the D0193 contract mechanism used as designed, application note riding its marker); the guard-45 emitted list matches. VERIFIED LIVE: the same advisable command fired twice read back issued 2 / repeated 1 / heed 50 percent - the first non-vacuous advisory measurement this repo has ever produced; suite 10/10; clippy clean after a line-budget extraction."; }
        part storyAdvisoryInstrumentationDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "130ac19e-2c9d-47da-b368-0a0406911f6f"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "d6c341701aefa9bf1cad16c900bc6391cf24f305"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-23"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeFable5"; }
    }

