    verification advisoryInstrumentationReviewGate : Test { :>> id = "d5b41026-3c4d-4cce-8aef-24c400e1bed3"; :>> title = "Sprint 433 review gate — three passes per D0172"; :>> createdAt = "2026-08-23"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "PASS 1, CLAIMS: probe outputs quoted from this session. PASS 2, BOUNDARY: the heed rate is an UPPER bound - an advisory followed by never re-running the command counts as heeded even if the agent simply moved on; the report's own note says so, and D0197's revisit reads the repeat count (the hard signal), not the rate. PASS 3, OWN DIFF: the first probe used commands the inspector does not flag (silent = no event, correctly) - the lesson is to probe with the control's own positive fixture, which the second attempt did. WHAT A REVIEWER SHOULD ATTACK: per-session last-advice state under .keel/metrics is machine-local, so the repeat signal does not aggregate across machines - the same D0180 named-consumer boundary, inherited, stated."; }
